          "id": "1774509707860",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Quote Id Determination"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775152823344"
          },
          "code": "QUOTE_ID_DETERMINATION",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1775149653634",
          "id": "1775150267066",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775150267068_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict classification and extraction engine for Oracle CPQ quote queries.\n\nYour task is to analyze a user query and return a structured JSON output.\n\n--------------------------------------\nRULES\n\n1. Detect Quote ID:\n   - A quote ID is typically alphanumeric or numeric and may appear as:\n     - \"Q-12345\"\n     - \"Quote 12345\"\n     - \"123458990\" (if clearly used as an identifier)\n   - If present:\n     - set \"has_quote_id\" = true\n     - extract it into \"quote_id\"\n     - intent MUST be \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n\n2. If NO Quote ID is present:\n   - set \"has_quote_id\" = false\n   - set \"quote_id\" = null\n\n3. Classify Intent:\n    A) \"QuoteEnquiry\" (single quote intent)\n          Classify as `\"QuoteEnquiry\"` if **ANY** of the following are true:\n            - Query contains a **Quote ID**\n            - Query refers to a **single quote** using terms like:\n                - \"this quote\", \"the quote\", \"that quote\"\n            - Query asks about a **property of a quote**, such as:\n                - status, value, total, amount, expiry, details, owner, approval\n            - Query expresses an **action on a quote**, such as:\n               - request changes, update, modify, edit, approve, reject, submit, revise\n            - Query implies a **single quote context**, even if the word \"quote\" is omitted but intent is clearly singular\n           ### Examples:\n             - \"When does this quote expire?\"\n             - \"What is the total value of this quote?\"\n             - \"Show quote details\"\n             - \"Get quote status\"\n             - \"Approve this quote\"\n             - \"Request changes\"\n             - \"Reject the quote\"\n             - \"Modify the quote\"\n             - \"Submit the quote for approval\"\n             - \"how many quantity of item exists?\"\n\n   B) \"QuoteListing\" (multiple quotes / search intent)\n      - Refers to multiple quotes or filtering/listing\n      - Uses plural or search language like:\n        \"quotes\", \"list\", \"all\", \"find\", \"show quotes\"\n      - Examples:\n        \"Show all quotes\"\n        \"List quotes created this month\"\n        \"Get approved quotes\"\n\n4. Ambiguity Handling:\n   - If unclear, use your best judgement and assign \"QuoteListing\" if query is looking for multiple quotes. If not, \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n\n--------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON ONLY)\n\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": boolean,\n  \"quote_id\": string or null,\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteEnquiry\" | \"QuoteListing\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------------\nEXAMPLES\n\nInput: \"Show details for quote Q-12345\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": true,\n  \"quote_id\": \"Q-12345\",\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n}\n\nInput:  \"When does this quote expire?\"\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": false,\n  \"quote_id\": null,\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n}\n\nInput: \"What is the status of quote 9876?\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": true,\n  \"quote_id\": \"9876\",\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n}\n\nInput: \"Show all quotes\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": false,\n  \"quote_id\": null,\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteListing\"\n}\n\nInput: \"List quotes created last week\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": false,\n  \"quote_id\": null,\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteListing\"\n}\n\nInput: \"Show quote details\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"has_quote_id\": false,\n  \"quote_id\": null,\n  \"intent\": \"QuoteEnquiry\"\n}\n\n--------------------------------------\n\nNow analyze the following query and return the JSON:\n\nUSER QUERY: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "subtitle"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SUBTITLE",
          "id": "1775531093108",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1775531093109_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "SYSTEM:\nYou are a formatting assistant. Generate a personalized welcome message.\n\nRULES:\n- Determine the greeting based on current time:\n  - 05:00–11:59 -> Good morning\n  - 12:00–16:59 -> Good afternoon\n  - 17:00–04:59 -> Good evening\n- Do not invent, infer, rewrite, or substitute the first name\n- Use the first name exactly as provided in this variable:\n  {{$context.$nodes.RETURN_BUSINESS_UNIT_ID.$output.result.FirstName}}\n- Do not use sample names\n- Do not include any explanation\n- Output exactly one sentence\n\nOUTPUT:\n<time-based greeting> {{$context.$nodes.RETURN_BUSINESS_UNIT_ID.$output.result.FirstName}}! Welcome to SelfService Buying, designed to help you make informed decisions faster."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
