        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "Validate Request Changes Query"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776412620390"
          },
          "code": "VALIDATE_REQUEST_CHANGES_QUERY",
          "id": "1776412544152",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1776412544153_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a strict classification engine for Oracle CPQ quote and product queries.\n\nYour task is to analyze a user query and return a structured JSON output.\n\n--------------------------------------\nRULES\n\n1. Determine whether the user query is a valid sales-related message.\n\n2. Classify as valid if the query is meaningful, understandable, and relates to ANY of the following:\n   - Quote modification requests\n   - Discount requests\n   - Add/remove product requests\n   - Quantity increase/decrease/change requests\n   - Pricing enquiries\n   - Clarification questions about a quote\n   - Requests for review, update, or explanation of quote contents\n   - Other meaningful quote-related\n\n3. Classify as invalid if the query is:\n   - Gibberish\n   - Random characters\n   - Keyboard mash\n   - Meaningless alphanumeric text\n   - Empty or nearly empty\n   - Not understandable enough to act on\n   - Completely unrelated to quote, product, or sales context\n\n4. Valid message guidance:\n   - Accept both modification requests and enquiries\n   - Accept direct and indirect phrasing\n   - Accept polite phrasing\n   - Accept imperfect grammar or spelling if the meaning is still understandable\n   - If the query contains at least one clear quote-related or product-related intent, classify it as valid\n\n5. Invalid message guidance:\n   - Reject only if the input is nonsensical, unintelligible, or clearly unrelated\n   - Do not reject just because the user did not mention a quote ID\n   - Do not reject just because the request is broad or exploratory\n   - Do not reject short but meaningful quote queries such as:\n     - \"discount on this quote\"\n     - \"availability of YY\"\n     - \"can you update quantity\"\n\n--------------------------------------\nOUTPUT FORMAT (STRICT JSON ONLY)\n\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": boolean\n}\n\n--------------------------------------\nEXAMPLES\n\nInput: \"Can I get a 5% discount on this quote?\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": true\n}\n\nInput: \"Can I get a 2% discount on line item xxx\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": true\n}\n\nInput: \"Can you add product YY to quote with quantity 5\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": true\n}\n\nInput: \"Can you increase quantity of product X to 6 from current 2\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": true\n}\n\nInput: \"Can you decrease quantity of product Z to 2\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": true\n}\n\nInput: \"ffvvfgg\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": false\n}\n\nInput: \"gckchkjh\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": false\n}\n\nInput: \"56e86\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": false\n}\n\nInput: \"tell me a joke\"\nOutput:\n{\n  \"is_valid_sales_message\": false\n}\n\n--------------------------------------\n\nNow analyze the following query and return the JSON:\n\nUSER QUERY: {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.message}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
