          "metadata": {
            "name": "Reject Quote Form"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "REJECT_QUOTE_FORM",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773649630204",
          "id": "1773324721001",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773324721007_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a UI generator agent. Create a single editable recordWidget form to collect the reason for rejecting a quote.\n\nInput:\n- Action context IDs: ID = {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}, TID = {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}\n\nForm requirements:\n1) Form metadata\n- Use recordWidget\n- Properties must include ONLY: id, readOnly, fields (no other top-level properties in the recordWidget payload)\n- id: \"rejectQuote~~<ID>~~<TID>\" where:\n  - <ID> is {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}\n  - <TID> is {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}\n- readOnly: false\n\n2) Fields (single column, stacked vertically)\n- Field A (Reason for Rejection)\n  - id: \"rejectPrompt~~<ID>~~<TID>\"\n  - description: \"You're about to reject this quote. Provide a reason for rejection to proceed. Once rejected, you will no longer be able to perform any further actions on it\"\n  - type: \"textarea\"\n  - label: \"Reason for Rejection *\"\n  - value: \"\" (an empty string)\n\n3) Strict constraints\n- Use the ids exactly as written, including the double tildes (~~); do not change case, punctuation, or separators.\n- Do not add any extra keys to the recordWidget properties beyond id, readOnly, fields.\n- Do not add extra field keys like placeholder, help, required, options, etc.\n- Do not emit JSON or any wrapper markup in this response unless required by your renderer. The platform will handle wrapping/formatting.\n- The textarea field’s value must be an empty string (\"\").\n\n4) Widget/layout guidance (non-binding if your renderer lacks layout controls)\n- Widget title: \"Reject Quote\"\n- Widget description: \"You're about to reject this quote. Provide a reason for rejection to proceed. Once rejected, you will no longer be able to perform any further actions on it\"\n- Place this form in a standard, single-column layout.\n\n5) User-facing message (must be shown outside the form; do not include inside the recordWidget properties)\n- Display this exact message prominently near the form:\n  \"You're about to reject this quote. Provide a reason for rejection to proceed. Once rejected, you will no longer be able to perform any further actions on it\"\n\nAdditional constraints (must enforce)\n- Use the ids exactly as written (including double tildes ~~, case, punctuation). Do not normalize or change them.\n- The textarea field’s value must be an empty string (\"\").\n- Do not add options (only valid for select fields).\n- Do not add extra field keys (no placeholder, help, required, etc.).\n- Validate final JSON (double-quoted strings, no trailing commas). If any check fails, regenerate until all checks pass.\n\nUser-facing message handling\n- Do not include any user notification inside the JSON. The platform will display this separately:\n  \"You're about to reject this quote. Provide a reason for rejection to proceed. Once rejected, you will no longer be able to perform any further actions on it\""
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
