          "metadata": {
            "name": "Display Billing and Shipping Addresses"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_BILLING_AND_SHIPPING_ADDRESSES",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773313953386",
          "id": "1772003255825",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772003255826_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a UI generator agent. From the input provided, extract the \"shippingMethods\", \"shippingAddresses\" and \"billingAddresses\" arrays and render a single editable recordWidget form with three single-select fields (Shipping Methods, Shipping Address, Billing Address, and Payment Method).\n\nInput:\n- ShippingMethods: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_ADDRESS_OBJECT.$output.result.shippingMethods}} \n- ShippingAddresses: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_ADDRESS_OBJECT.$output.result.shippingAddresses}} \n- BillingAddresses: {{$context.$nodes.PREPARE_ADDRESS_OBJECT.$output.result.billingAddresses}} \n- Action context IDs: ID = {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}, TID = {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}\n\n\nForm requirements:\n1) Form metadata\n- Use recordWidget\n- id: \"order_totals_form~~<ID>~~<TID>\" where:\n    - <ID> is {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}\n    - <TID> is {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}\n- readOnly: false\n- Submit button label: set to \"Checkout\" (use the property submitText: \"Checkout\"; if submitText is not supported by the renderer, still label the button in the UI as \"Checkout\")\n\n2) Fields (all fields belong to this same recordWidget and are they must be stacked/arranged vertically.)\n- Field A (Billing Address)\n  - id: \"billing_address\"\n  - type: \"select\"\n  - label: \"Billing Address\"\n  - options: Build from the BillingAddresses array\n    - For each array item:\n       - value: \"<value>\" using the item's value\n       - label: \"<label>\" using the item's label\n  - value: Pick the default item from the options\n\n- Field B (Shipping Address)\n  - id: \"shipping_address\"\n  - type: \"select\"\n  - label: \"Shipping Address\"\n  - options: Build from the ShippingAddresses array (same value/label rules as Billing)\n       - value: \"<value>\" using the item's value\n       - label: \"<label>\" using the item's label\n  - value: Pick the default item from the options.\n\n- Field C (Shipping Method)\n  - id: \"shipping_method\"\n  - type: \"select\"\n  - label: \"Shipping Method\"\n  - options: Build from the ShippingMethods array\n     - For each array item:\n       - value: \"<value>\" using the item's value\n       - label: \"<label>\" using the item's label\n  - value: default to the first item in this options array, if present\n\n- Field D (Payment Method)\n  - id: \"payment_method\"\n  - type: \"select\"\n  - label: \"Payment Method\"\n  - options: a single option\n    - { \"value\": \"INVOICE\", \"label\": \"Invoice\" }\n  - value: \"INVOICE\"\n\n3) Page/layout rules\n- Page title should be \"Order\"\n- The entire form container should occupy 8 columns horizontally (if your layout system supports column spans, set the container width to 8 of 12 columns; otherwise, size the form to approximate two-thirds width)\n- All three selects must be part of this same recordWidget and appear in a single vertical stack (one per row)"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Checkout Prompt Extractor",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "return $context.$nodes.DISPLAY_BILLING_AND_SHIPPING_ADDRESSES.$input.prompt;"
