          },
          "code": "RESPONSEROUTER",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1773312815689",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773312815690_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.IDENTIFYMODE.$output.result === \"ui\"}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": false,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Compare Rate Plans UI"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "COMPARE_RATE_PLANS_UI",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773314219091",
          "id": "1772627454649",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1772627454652_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Inputs:\n- `ratePlans`: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RATE_PLANS.$output}}\n- `charges`: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_RATE_PLAN_CHARGES_LOOP.$output}}\n- `document`: {{$context.$nodes.FETCH_DOCUMENT_DETAILS.$output.documents}}\n- `transactionId`: {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}\n- `quoteId`: {{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}\n- `currency`: {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_CURRENCY.$output.result?.currency}}\n\nDirective: Use the provided input data to render a `multiRecordWidget` comparison of available rate plans. Treat the sample shapes in `rate-plans/data.json` only as structural reference. Runtime values will differ, but the input structure will remain the same. Map values directly from the four runtime inputs and arithmetic derived from those inputs only. Do not invent values, fill gaps with assumptions, or borrow values from unrelated sections of input.\n\nAdditional input:\n- `CustomerPersona`: {{$context.$app.$OraAppContext}}\n  - Allowed values: `Procurement Manager` | `Finance Manager` | `CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)` | `Field Ops Manager`\n  - If missing or unrecognized, use `Procurement Manager`.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Procurement Manager\"\n- Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n- Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n- Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction renewals.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Finance Manager\"\n- Goal: Optimize budget adherence and cash predictability while minimizing financial leakage (unplanned spend, overruns, avoidable fees).\n- Priorities: Total cost visibility (TCV/annual/one-time), budget timing, payment terms, invoice accuracy, discount realization, forecasting.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer options that reduce variance and improve financial control (clear cost drivers, predictable billing, defensible ROI).\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"CustomerExecutiveOffice (CXO)\"\n- Goal: Achieve business outcomes and reduce enterprise risk through reliable delivery, measurable value, and strategic alignment.\n- Priorities: Business impact, risk posture, executive-level visibility, time-to-value, scalability, vendor accountability, strategic fit.\n- Decision Lens: Choose the option that maximizes outcomes and reduces material risk; prioritize simplicity, speed, and clear accountability.\n\n### If CustomerPersona == \"Field Ops Manager\"\n- Goal: Maintain uptime and operational readiness by ensuring teams have what they need when they need it.\n- Priorities: Availability/lead time, service continuity, entitlements/access, deployment readiness, support responsiveness, minimizing downtime.\n- Decision Lens: Prefer choices that reduce operational friction and outage risk; prioritize fast execution, clear ownership, and practical deliverability.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nINPUT STRUCTURE REFERENCE\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUse these shapes as the only structural contract. Do not require exact sample values.\n\n1) `ratePlans` structure:\n- `ratePlans` is an array of plan objects\n- each plan object may contain:\n  - `number`\n  - `integrationId`\n  - `description`\n  - `label`\n\n2) `charges` structure:\n- `charges` is an object\n- rate-plan charge details are read from `charges.lines[0]` in this context\n- `charges.lines` is an array, but for this prompt assume the relevant payload is the first item when present\n- `charges.lines[0]` may contain:\n  - `appliedRatePlanNumber`\n  - `appliedRatePlanLabel`\n  - `appliedRatePlanIntegrationId`\n  - `_partNumber`\n  - `_itemIdentifier`\n  - `_bomItemVariableName`\n  - `charges`\n- `charges.lines[0].charges` is the array of charge objects to use for calculations\n\n1) `document`\n- only these fields are relevant for this widget when present:\n  - `transactionID_l`\n  - `_sequence_number`\n  - `_line_display_name`\n  - `_part_number`\n  - `_requestedRatePlan.value`\n  - `_requestedRatePlan.displayValue`\n\n1) `transactionId`:\n- `transactionId` is a standalone string input\n- it is used only as heading context text when present\n\nIf a value is absent at runtime, omit dependent wording or action fields rather than guessing.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nSOURCE OF TRUTH RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n1) Available plans source:\n- Use only `ratePlans`.\n- Create exactly one row per available plan, preserving the input order.\n- Empty-data guardrail:\n  - First determine whether available plans exist.\n  - Treat `ratePlans` as having no available plans when it is missing, null, not an array, or an array with length `0`.\n  - If there are no available plans, stop. Do not evaluate charges, do not compute totals, do not compare plans, and do not infer rows from `document`, `transactionId`, `quoteId`, or any other input.\n  - In that case, return a valid `multiRecordWidget` with the required columns and `config.rows = []`.\n  - Do not create synthetic placeholder rows such as guessed plan names, `No Rate Plans` rows, or fake status rows.\n  - The empty state must be represented only by the empty `rows` array plus a truthful subtitle.\n\n2) Current plan source:\n- `currentPlanNumber = document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.value`\n- Use `document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.value` for all logic, matching, and current-plan comparisons.\n- Use `document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.displayValue` only when displaying the selected/current plan name in UI wording.\n\n3) Charges source:\n- For each plan, use only `charges.lines[0].charges`.\n- In this context, `charges.lines` will contain one item, and that first item is the only relevant charge payload.\n- If `charges.lines[0]` is missing or `charges.lines[0].charges` is not an array, use an empty `charges` array for that plan.\n- Use `charges.lines[0].appliedRatePlanNumber` only as contextual metadata when present; do not search across multiple payloads.\n- Never use any fields outside `charges.lines[0].charges` for plan comparison math.\n- Never reuse charges from one plan for another plan.\n\n4) Document source for actions and heading context:\n- Use only these fields when present:\n  - `transactionId`\n  - `document.document.documents.transactionID_l`\n  - `document.document.documents._sequence_number`\n  - `document.document.documents._line_display_name`\n  - `document.document.documents._part_number`\n  - `document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.value`\n  - `document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.displayValue`\n- Do not read from any alternate transaction object path.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nMANDATORY INPUT SANITIZATION\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSanitize `charges` before any calculations.\n\n1) Normalize top-level value into `sourceEntries`:\n- If `charges.lines` is an array and `charges.lines[0]` is an object, use `charges.lines[0]` as `sourceEntry`.\n- Else use `null`.\n\n2) Parse the source entry safely into `parsedChargePayload`:\n- If `sourceEntry` is an object, candidate = sourceEntry.\n- Else candidate = null.\n\n3) Accept only a valid plan payload:\n- If `candidate.charges` is not an array, replace it with `[]`\n- If `candidate` is null, use an empty `charges` array\n\n4) Numeric sanitization:\n- For every `extendedAmount` and `unitPrice`, use `Number(value)`.\n- If result is not finite, treat it as `0`.\n- Keep raw numeric precision during calculations.\n- Round only when formatting display strings.\nDo not substitute values from `document`, `transactionId`, `ratePlans`, or any other source when `charges.lines[0].charges` is present.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nMULTIRECORD WIDGET SCHEMA RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nUse the valid `multiRecordWidget` structure:\n- Widget type: `multiRecordWidget`\n- `config.subtitle`: string\n- `config.cols`: array of strings\n- `config.rows`: array of row objects\n- Each row object must contain `cells`\n- Each row may optionally contain `action`\n- Each row `cells` array may contain strings and one badge object\n\nBadge cell shape:\n`{ \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": string, \"priority\": \"alert\"|\"warning\"|\"medium\"|\"success\" }`\n\nAction shape:\n`{ \"text\": string, \"command\": string }`\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nREQUIRED COLUMNS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n`config.cols` must be exactly this array in this exact order:\n[\n  \"Rate Plan\",\n  \"Upfront\",\n  \"Monthly\",\n  \"Annual Run-rate\",\n  \"Variable Usage Rates\",\n  \"Status\"\n]\n\nBecause `multiRecordWidget` rows must align with columns, each row must contain exactly 6 cells in the same order above.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nDETERMINISTIC CHARGE BUCKETING\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor each plan, evaluate only `charges.lines[0].charges`.\n\nBucket precedence for each individual charge:\n1. If `priceType == \"One Time\"` => add sanitized `unitPrice` to `upfrontTotal`\n2. Else if `priceType == \"Recurring\"` AND `pricePeriod == \"Per Month\"` => add sanitized `unitPrice` to `recurringMonthly`\n3. Else if `priceType == \"Recurring\"` AND `pricePeriod == \"Per Year\"` => add sanitized `unitPrice` to `recurringYearly`\n4. Else if `priceType == \"Usage\"`:\n   - if lowercase `usageUOM` contains `min`, add sanitized `unitPrice` to `usageRatePerMin`\n   - if lowercase `usageUOM` contains `gb`, add sanitized `unitPrice` to `usageRatePerGB`\n   - otherwise ignore that usage charge\n5. Else ignore the charge\n\nMandatory isolation rules:\n- A charge contributes to exactly one bucket.\n- Include all matching charges regardless of `isProductPrice`, `chargeType`, or `chargeDefinition`.\n- Never place Usage charges in recurring buckets.\n- Never place One Time charges in recurring buckets.\n- Never place Recurring charges in the upfront bucket.\n- If a Recurring charge has missing or unknown `pricePeriod`, ignore it.\n- For usage scenarios, always use `unitPrice`, never `extendedAmount`.\n- Never use line-level document pricing fields such as `netAmount_l`, `netPrice_l`, `listAmount_l`, `listPrice_l`, or similar rollups to populate table values.\n- Never infer Monthly, Annual Run-rate, or Upfront values from the current document line. Those fields describe the current document context and can differ from matched plan charge payloads.\n- When `charges.lines[0]` exists, its `charges` array is the only allowed source for displayed cost values.\n\nInterpretation note for this dataset shape:\n- `extendedAmount` values in matched plan charges may represent multi-period totals.\n- `unitPrice` values represent the per-period rate for the individual charge.\n- Therefore:\n  - use `unitPrice` for the `Upfront` column when `priceType == \"One Time\"`\n  - use `unitPrice` for monthly recurring charge aggregation when `priceType == \"Recurring\"` and `pricePeriod == \"Per Month\"`\n  - use `unitPrice` for yearly recurring charge aggregation when `priceType == \"Recurring\"` and `pricePeriod == \"Per Year\"`\n  - use `unitPrice` for usage rates when `priceType == \"Usage\"`\n- Ignore `extendedAmount` when computing displayed Monthly, Annual Run-rate, Upfront, or Variable Usage Rates values for this widget.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nCALCULATIONS\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFor each plan:\n- `monthlyFixedEffective = recurringMonthly + (recurringYearly / 12)`\n- `year1FixedTotal = recurringYearly + (recurringMonthly * 12)`\n\nImportant:\n- `year1FixedTotal` must NOT include `upfrontTotal`.\n- `upfrontTotal` is shown only in the `Upfront` column.\n- For recurring charges, derive `recurringMonthly` and `recurringYearly` from `unitPrice`, not `extendedAmount`, so the Monthly column reflects the actual per-month rate and the Annual Run-rate reflects the first-year recurring run rate.\n- For One Time charges, derive `upfrontTotal` from `unitPrice`, not `extendedAmount`.\n- Concretely for this rate-plan comparison:\n  - `upfrontTotal = sum(unitPrice where priceType == \"One Time\")`\n  - `recurringMonthly = sum(unitPrice where priceType == \"Recurring\" and pricePeriod == \"Per Month\")`\n  - `recurringYearly = sum(unitPrice where priceType == \"Recurring\" and pricePeriod == \"Per Year\")`\n- Do not average, prorate, annualize, divide, or otherwise transform `extendedAmount` to derive Monthly values.\n- Do not mix `unitPrice` from some recurring charges with `extendedAmount` from other recurring charges in the same plan.\n- For the Monthly column, sum only recurring `unitPrice` values that belong in the recurring buckets defined above.\n- For the Annual Run-rate column, use only `recurringYearly + recurringMonthly * 12` derived from recurring `unitPrice` values.\n- Never divide a recurring `extendedAmount` by 12 or by contract term to derive displayed monthly values.\n- `hasUsageCharges = usageRatePerMin > 0 OR usageRatePerGB > 0`\n\nRecommendation logic:\n- Do not invent low, medium, high, or any assumed customer usage scenarios.\n- Do not rank plans using guessed usage volumes.\n- If usage charges exist for any plan, do not claim one plan is definitively best overall unless the comparison can be made from fixed charges alone without ambiguity.\n- Base comparison only on known recurring and one-time charges present in `charges.lines[0].charges`.\n\nStatus booleans:\n- `isCurrent = (plan.number === currentPlanNumber)`\n- `isLowestFixedCostPlan = plan has the minimum year1FixedTotal among available plans`\n- `hasUsageSensitivity = hasUsageCharges`\n\nStatus intent:\n- `CURRENT` should identify the currently applied plan.\n- `OPTION` should identify all non-current plans by default.\n- Use `RECOMMENDED` only when recommendation is supportable from known fixed-charge data without relying on assumed customer usage.\n- If usage-based uncertainty exists and fixed charges alone do not justify a clear recommendation, do not label any non-current plan as `RECOMMENDED`.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nDISPLAY FORMATTING RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nFormat all currency values using the input `currency` value with:\n- `<currency>` prefix\n- thousands separators\n- exactly 2 decimals\n\nCell mapping per row:\n1. `Rate Plan`:\n   - use `plan.label` if it is a non-empty string\n   - otherwise use `plan.number`\n2. `Upfront`:\n   - `\"<currency> <upfrontTotal>\"`\n3. `Monthly`:\n   - `\"<currency> <monthlyFixedEffective>/mo\"`\n4. `Annual Run-rate`:\n   - `\"<currency> <year1FixedTotal>\"`\n5. `Variable Usage Rates`:\n   - if both usage rates are zero: `\"<currency> 0.00 usage\"`\n   - otherwise always show both sides: `\"<currency> <usageRatePerMin>/min + <currency> <usageRatePerGB>/GB\"`\n6. `Status`:\n   - must be the badge object, not a string\n\nStatus badge logic:\n- If `isCurrent`:\n  - `{ \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"CURRENT\", \"priority\": \"medium\" }`\n- Else:\n  - `{ \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"OPTION\", \"priority\": \"warning\" }`\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nHEADING/SUBTITLE AND PERSONA-SAFE WORDING\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n**Use the following mappings to set root widget's title and description properties**\n### root-widget properties\n#### title\n- Combine <quoteName> from `transactionId`, <partName> from `document.document.documents._line_display_name`, and <selectedRatePlan> from `document.document.documents._requestedRatePlan.displayValue` in the following manner to generate a meaningful title and set it to root widget's `title` property:\n```\n<quoteName> | Compare alternatives to <selectedRatePlan> for <partName>\n```\n#### description\n- Set the root widget's `description` property to the following: \n```\n\"Review the detailed breakdown of alternative plans. You can choose to keep your existing rate plan or switch to a new one\"\n```\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nACTION RULES\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nInclude row `action` only for non-current plans.\n\nWhen action is allowed:\n- `action.text = \"Update\"`\n- `action.command = ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", \"<action>~~<transactionId>~~<quoteId>~~<documentNumber>~~<requested_rate_plan>\")`\n\nToken mapping:\n- `<action>` = \"Details\"\n- `<quoteId>` = `quoteId`\n- `<transactionId>` = `transactionId`\n- `<documentNumber>` = `String(document._document_number)`\n- `<requested_rate_plan>` = current row `plan.number`\n\nBefore adding action, verify every token above is present and non-empty after string conversion.\n- If any token is missing, empty, null, or undefined, omit the action for that row.\n- If the built command would contain an empty token between separators or contains `~~~~~~~~`, omit the action.\n- Never emit placeholder braces like `{{transaction_id}}` in final output.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------\nFINAL VALIDATION CHECKLIST\n----------------------------------------------------------------\n\nBefore output, verify all of the following:\n\n1) Output structure:\n- The response is a valid `multiRecordWidget`\n- It contains `config`\n\n2) Columns and rows:\n- `config.cols` matches the exact 6 labels above in exact order\n- If `ratePlans` is a valid non-empty array, number of rows equals number of `ratePlans`\n- If `ratePlans` is missing, not an array, or empty, `config.rows` must be an empty array\n- Every row has exactly 6 cells\n- Cell #6 in every row is a valid badge object\n\n3) Numeric consistency per plan:\n- `monthlyFixedEffective == recurringMonthly + recurringYearly / 12`\n- `year1FixedTotal == recurringYearly + recurringMonthly * 12`\n- If any check fails, recompute from sanitized `charges.lines[0].charges` before formatting\n\n4) Data provenance:\n- No displayed value comes from unmatched plan charges\n- No displayed value comes from outside `charges.lines[0].charges`\n- No displayed value comes from `ratePlans` charge-like paths\n- No displayed value comes from document line pricing rollups\n- No heading text comes from any unsupported object path\n- No missing source value is guessed or invented\n- In the no-plans case, no row values, pricing values, actions, or badges are inferred from any source\n\n5) Actions:\n- Current row has no action\n- Non-current rows have action only if all tokens are complete\n- No action command contains empty separators or placeholders\n\nIf any rule conflicts with another rule, prioritize in this order:\n1. Return a valid `multiRecordWidget`\n2. Use only traceable input data and direct arithmetic from it\n3. Preserve exact schema and exact column order\n4. Preserve deterministic plan matching and charge isolation\n5. Omit optional fields rather than guessing"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
