        {
          "metadata": {
            "errorNodeId": "1768190969668",
            "name": "Format Preview Order Totals",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const totalsResponse = $context.$nodes.FETCH_SHIPPING_AND_TAX.$output;\n\nconst toNumber = (value) => {\n  const numericValue = Number(value ?? 0);\n  return Number.isFinite(numericValue) ? numericValue : 0;\n};\n\nconst roundCurrency = (value) => Math.round((toNumber(value) + Number.EPSILON) * 100) / 100;\n\nconst formatMoney = (value, currencyCode = 'USD') => {\n  const amount = roundCurrency(value);\n\n  try {\n    return new Intl.NumberFormat('en-US', {\n      style: 'currency',\n      currency: currencyCode,\n      minimumFractionDigits: 2,\n      maximumFractionDigits: 2,\n    }).format(amount);\n  } catch (error) {\n    return `${currencyCode} ${amount.toFixed(2)}`;\n  }\n};\n\nconst sumAmounts = (items = [], selector) => roundCurrency(items.reduce((total, item) => total + toNumber(selector(item)), 0));\n\nconst getExtendedAmount = (component) => component?.HeaderCurrencyExtendedAmount?.Value ?? component?.ExtendedAmount?.Value ?? 0;\n\nconst normalizeChargeType = (chargeTypeCode = '') => {\n  if (chargeTypeCode === 'ORA_SALE') {\n    return 'LINE_TOTAL';\n  }\n\n  if (chargeTypeCode.includes('SHIPPING')) {\n    return 'SHIPPING';\n  }\n\n  return chargeTypeCode || 'OTHER';\n};\n\nconst buildTaxDetailsForLine = (lineComponents = [], taxLineDetails = [], currencyCode = 'USD') => {\n  const taxDetailsByChargeComponentId = taxLineDetails.reduce((accumulator, taxDetail) => {\n    const key = taxDetail.ChargeComponentId;\n\n    if (!accumulator[key]) {\n      accumulator[key] = [];\n    }\n\n    accumulator[key].push(taxDetail);\n    return accumulator;\n  }, {});\n\n  const exclusiveTaxComponents = lineComponents.filter((component) => component.PriceElementUsageCode === 'EXCLUSIVE_TAX');\n\n  return exclusiveTaxComponents.map((component) => {\n    const matchedTaxLines = taxDetailsByChargeComponentId[component.ChargeComponentId] ?? [];\n    const taxRate = matchedTaxLines[0]?.TaxRate ?? null;\n    const taxCode = matchedTaxLines[0]?.TaxRateCode ?? matchedTaxLines[0]?.TaxRateName ?? null;\n    const taxableAmount = sumAmounts(matchedTaxLines, (taxDetail) => taxDetail?.HeaderCurrencyTaxableAmount?.Value ?? taxDetail?.TaxableAmount?.Value ?? 0);\n    const taxAmount = getExtendedAmount(component);\n\n    return {\n      chargeComponentId: component.ChargeComponentId,\n      taxCode,\n      taxRate,\n      taxableAmount,\n      taxableAmountDisplay: formatMoney(taxableAmount, currencyCode),\n      taxAmount,\n      taxAmountDisplay: formatMoney(taxAmount, currencyCode),\n      explanation: component.Explanation ?? null,\n    };\n  });\n};\n\nconst buildLineSummaries = (lines = [], chargesByLine = {}, componentsByChargeId = {}, taxLineDetails = [], currencyCode = 'USD') => lines.map((line) => {\n  const lineCharges = chargesByLine[line.LineId] ?? [];\n  const lineComponents = lineCharges.flatMap((charge) => componentsByChargeId[charge.ChargeId] ?? []);\n  const taxDetails = buildTaxDetailsForLine(lineComponents, taxLineDetails, currencyCode);\n  const lineTotal = sumAmounts(\n    lineComponents.filter((component) => component.PriceElementUsageCode === 'NET_PRICE' && component.ChargeId && lineCharges.some((charge) => charge.ChargeId === component.ChargeId && charge.ChargeTypeCode === 'ORA_SALE')),\n    getExtendedAmount,\n  );\n  const shippingTotal = sumAmounts(\n    lineComponents.filter((component) => component.PriceElementUsageCode === 'NET_PRICE' && component.ChargeId && lineCharges.some((charge) => charge.ChargeId === component.ChargeId && normalizeChargeType(charge.ChargeTypeCode) === 'SHIPPING')),\n    getExtendedAmount,\n  );\n  const taxTotal = sumAmounts(lineComponents.filter((component) => component.PriceElementUsageCode === 'EXCLUSIVE_TAX'), getExtendedAmount);\n  const orderTotal = roundCurrency(lineTotal + shippingTotal + taxTotal);\n\n  return {\n    lineId: line.LineId,\n    itemNumber: line.InventoryItemNumber ?? `Line ${line.LineId}`,\n    quantity: toNumber(line?.LineQuantity?.Value),\n    uom: line?.LineQuantity?.UomCode ?? line.LineQuantityUOMCode ?? null,\n    taxClassificationCode: line.TaxClassificationCode ?? null,\n    lineTotal,\n    lineTotalDisplay: formatMoney(lineTotal, currencyCode),\n    shippingTotal,\n    shippingTotalDisplay: formatMoney(shippingTotal, currencyCode),\n    taxTotal,\n    taxTotalDisplay: formatMoney(taxTotal, currencyCode),\n    orderTotal,\n    orderTotalDisplay: formatMoney(orderTotal, currencyCode),\n    taxDetails,\n  };\n});\n\nconst formatPricingTotals = (pricingResponse = {}) => {\n  const header = pricingResponse.Header?.[0] ?? {};\n  const lines = pricingResponse.Line ?? [];\n  const charges = pricingResponse.Charge ?? [];\n  const components = pricingResponse.ChargeComponent ?? [];\n  const taxLineDetails = pricingResponse.TaxLineDetail ?? [];\n  const currencyCode = header.AppliedCurrencyCode ?? header.DefaultCurrencyCode ?? 'USD';\n\n  const chargesByLine = charges.reduce((accumulator, charge) => {\n    const lineId = charge.LineId ?? charge.ParentEntityId;\n\n    if (!accumulator[lineId]) {\n      accumulator[lineId] = [];\n    }\n\n    accumulator[lineId].push(charge);\n    return accumulator;\n  }, {});\n\n  const componentsByChargeId = components.reduce((accumulator, component) => {\n    if (!accumulator[component.ChargeId]) {\n      accumulator[component.ChargeId] = [];\n    }\n\n    accumulator[component.ChargeId].push(component);\n    return accumulator;\n  }, {});\n\n  const lineSummaries = buildLineSummaries(lines, chargesByLine, componentsByChargeId, taxLineDetails, currencyCode);\n  const totals = {\n    lineTotal: sumAmounts(lineSummaries, (line) => line.lineTotal),\n    shippingTotal: sumAmounts(lineSummaries, (line) => line.shippingTotal),\n    taxTotal: sumAmounts(lineSummaries, (line) => line.taxTotal),\n  };\n\n  totals.orderTotal = roundCurrency(totals.lineTotal + totals.shippingTotal + totals.taxTotal);\n\n  return {\n    pricingContext: pricingResponse.PricingServiceParameter?.[0]?.PricingContext ?? null,\n    status: pricingResponse.PricingServiceParameter?.[0]?.OutputStatus ?? null,\n    currencyCode,\n    priceAsOf: header.PriceAsOf ?? null,\n    pricedOn: header.PricedOn ?? null,\n    headerId: header.HeaderId ?? null,\n    lineCount: lineSummaries.length,\n    lineSummaries,\n    totals: {\n      lineTotal: totals.lineTotal,\n      lineTotalDisplay: formatMoney(totals.lineTotal, currencyCode),\n      shippingTotal: totals.shippingTotal,\n      shippingTotalDisplay: formatMoney(totals.shippingTotal, currencyCode),\n      taxTotal: totals.taxTotal,\n      taxTotalDisplay: formatMoney(totals.taxTotal, currencyCode),\n      orderTotal: totals.orderTotal,\n      orderTotalDisplay: formatMoney(totals.orderTotal, currencyCode),\n    },\n    displayRows: [\n      {\n        label: 'Line Total',\n        amount: totals.lineTotal,\n        amountDisplay: formatMoney(totals.lineTotal, currencyCode),\n        detail: `${lineSummaries.length} line${lineSummaries.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`,\n      },\n      {\n        label: 'Shipping',\n        amount: totals.shippingTotal,\n        amountDisplay: formatMoney(totals.shippingTotal, currencyCode),\n        detail: 'All shipping charges',\n      },\n      {\n        label: 'Tax',\n        amount: totals.taxTotal,\n        amountDisplay: formatMoney(totals.taxTotal, currencyCode),\n        detail: 'Exclusive tax',\n      },\n      {\n        label: 'Order Total',\n        amount: totals.orderTotal,\n        amountDisplay: formatMoney(totals.orderTotal, currencyCode),\n        detail: 'Line + shipping + tax',\n      },\n    ],\n    llmSummary: {\n      title: 'Order totals',\n      subtitle: `Pricing totals in ${currencyCode}`,\n      rows: [\n        ['Line Total', formatMoney(totals.lineTotal, currencyCode), `${lineSummaries.length} line${lineSummaries.length === 1 ? '' : 's'}`],\n        ['Shipping', formatMoney(totals.shippingTotal, currencyCode), 'All shipping charges'],\n        ['Tax', formatMoney(totals.taxTotal, currencyCode), 'Exclusive tax'],\n        ['Order Total', formatMoney(totals.orderTotal, currencyCode), 'Line + shipping + tax'],\n      ],\n    },\n  };\n};\n\nreturn formatPricingTotals(totalsResponse);"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1775820482992"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_PREVIEW_ORDER_TOTALS",
          "id": "1775132252074",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"additionalProperties\": false,\n  \"required\": [\n    \"result\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Quote Action Details"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUOTE_ACTION_DETAILS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1773314089716",
          "id": "1771935185661",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1771935185662_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a customer-facing sales assistant for a self-service quote experience. Represent your company professionally. Be respectful, persuasive, and helpful.\nUse only the provided quote data. Do not invent benefits, savings, objections, product claims, internal details, or next steps that are not directly supported by the input.\n\n## Input:\nQuote JSON: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_QUOTE_DETAILS.$output}}`\nQuote Row Metadata: `{{$context.$nodes.QUOTE_LINE_ITEMS_METADATA.$output.result}}`\nAction Details: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result}}`\nEligible Actions: `{{$context.$nodes.DETERMINE_QUOTE_ACTIONS.$output.result}}`\nTransaction Comments: `{{$context.$nodes.GET_TRANSACTION_COMMENTS.$output}}`\n\nDefine aliases for field references below:\n- `QUOTE` = the Quote JSON object above\n- All quote header fields are under: `QUOTE.documents`\n- `ROW_METADATA` = the Quote Row Metadata object above\n- `ROW_DATA` = `ROW_METADATA.rows`\n- `ROW_COLUMNS` = `ROW_METADATA.columns`\n\nAdditional input:\n- `CustomerPersona`: \"Procurement Manager\"\n\n## Persona Rules\nUse the persona only to adjust tone, emphasis, and decision framing.\nDo not change facts.\nDo not mention the persona label in the output.\nPersona Definition:\n- `Procurement Manager`:\n    - Goal: Ensure continuity of supply/service while maintaining pricing integrity and contract compliance.\n    - Priorities: Cost control, contract compliance, risk mitigation, renewal governance, supplier accountability.\n    - Decision Lens: Minimize commercial risk and operational disruption; favor clear terms, predictable pricing, and low-friction renewals.\n    - Summary tone emphasis: commercially disciplined, clear, dependable, continuity-focused.\n\n## Shared currency formatting rule\nWhen formatting a money object with fields `{ value, currency }`:\n- if the currency code is present and non-empty, prefix the formatted number with the currency code and a space (for example: `USD 123,456`)\n- if the currency field is missing or empty, output the numeric value only\n\n#### DATE FORMATTING\n- All dates MUST be formatted as: DD/MMM/YYYY\n- Day MUST be 2 digits (01–31)\n- Month MUST be a 3-letter uppercase abbreviation (JAN–DEC)\n- Year MUST be 4 digits\n- DO NOT include time or timezone information\n- If the input date is missing, null, or invalid → return an empty string (\"\")\n- NEVER output dates in any other format\n\n## 1) Summary paragraph\nWrite exactly one short customer-facing paragraph.\nRules:\n- Keep it strictly concise, targeting 3-4 sentences maximum.\n- Use a professional, welcoming tone.\n- Bold key elements such as the project/transaction name, current status, and the word \"assigned\" for quick scannability.\n- Do NOT use the words \"buyer\" or \"seller\" anywhere in the summary paragraph.\n- Focus on high-level customer-relevant context only, since contract values and detailed line items are already displayed below.\n- Do not repeat total contract value, discount amounts, final contract value, exact line-item pricing, or exhaustive line-item quantities in the paragraph.\n- Use `QUOTE.documents.transactionName_t` as the primary project/transaction reference when available.\n- Synthesize a brief overview of the quoted scope by looking at line items and grouping them naturally into business-friendly categories such as hardware, software, subscriptions, or services when supported by the data.\n- If `QUOTE.documents.contractedPeriods_t` exists, you may mention the contract duration at a high level.\n- Ignore all dates except `QUOTE.documents.priceExpirationDate_t`, and mention that date only if it falls within 14 days of the current date.\n- Treat the quote as a renewal only if `QUOTE.documents.renewDraftSubscriptionNumber_t` exists and is not empty.\n- If the quote is a renewal, acknowledge continuity of service and ongoing partnership. Do not frame it as net-new.\n- Current status rule (STRICT):\n  - Use ONLY `QUOTE.documents._s_customerStatus_t.displayValue` to indicate the current status/phase.\n  - Do NOT use any other fields (including assignment, internal statuses, or inferred stages) as a proxy for quote status.\n  - Do NOT use `QUOTE.documents.status_t` in the summary.\n- Assignment indicator (STRICT):\n  - The summary MUST include exactly one assignment clause using the word **assigned** (bold the word \"assigned\") if `_s_assignedTo_t.value` exists:\n    - If `_s_assignedTo_t.value` = `BUYER` → include: `and **assigned** to you for review`\n    - If `_s_assignedTo_t.value` = `SELLER` → include: `and **assigned** to our sales representative for review`\n    - Otherwise → omit any assignment clause.\n  - Do not add any other narrative about assignment.\n\nPreferred first-sentence template (use when fields exist):\n`The **<transactionName>** quote is currently in **<customerStatus>** status <assignment clause>.`\n\nIf `transactionName_t` is missing, omit the name and start with `The quote...`.\n- Do not mention blockers, risks, approvals, or internal next steps.\n- Do not read from or mention sales-rep-specific properties.\n- Omit unsupported details.\n\n## 2) Conversation summary paragraph\nWrite at most one additional short paragraph that summarizes relevant conversation history from `Transaction Comments`.\nRules:\n- Only use `Transaction Comments.items` when it exists and contains items.\n- Ignore any comment where `_s_isInternalComment` = `true`.\n- If no non-internal comments remain after filtering, output nothing for this section.\n- The paragraph must be customer-centric, concise, and directly relevant to the current quote discussion.\n- Output the conversation summary in italics as a single paragraph.\n- Do NOT use the words \"buyer\" or \"seller\". Refer to parties generically (e.g., \"you\", \"our team\") only if supported by the comments.\n- Focus on the most relevant open discussion points and recent decisions explicitly stated in the comments.\n- If older comments have already reached closure and do not add value, you may ignore them and summarize only what is still relevant now.\n- Do not add inferred \"alignment\" or negotiation states unless explicitly stated in the comments.\n- Do not expose internal-only discussions, seller-only reasoning, unsupported claims, or hidden process details.\n- Do not repeat the full quote summary.\n\n## 3) Contract value lines\nAfter the paragraph(s), output markdown value lines using these rules:\n- If `QUOTE.documents._s_customerStatus_t?.value === 'solutionDiscovery' || QUOTE.documents._s_customerStatus_t?.value === 'negotiation'`, omit this entire section and output nothing for Contract value lines.\n- Otherwise:\n  - If `QUOTE.documents.totalContractDiscount_t.value` is exactly `0`, output only:\n    - `**Final Contract Value:** {QUOTE.documents.totalContractValue_t.value}`\n  - Otherwise, output these markdown lines when values exist:\n    - `**Pre-Discount Contract Value:** {QUOTE.documents.totalContractListValue_t.value}`\n    - `**Discounted Amount Value:** {QUOTE.documents.totalContractDiscount_t.value}`\n    - `**Final Contract Value:** {QUOTE.documents.totalContractValue_t.value}`\nRules:\n- Use bold labels only.\n- Do not use a markdown table.\n- Format each monetary value using the shared currency formatting rule.\n- For example, if `totalContractValue_t.currency = \"USD\"`, format the value as `USD 18,262.50`.\n- If a monetary value is missing, omit that line.\n- Do not show discount percentage in this section.\n\n## 4) Line items using `multiRecordWidget`\nSource: `ROW_METADATA`\nIf `ROW_DATA` is missing, not an array, or empty:\n- Output exactly: `No line items are available.`\n- Do not output a widget.\n\nOtherwise output one App Builder display block for a `multiRecordWidget`.\nFollow the `multiRecordWidget` schema strictly: the widget must contain `properties.cols` and `properties.rows`, and each element of `properties.rows` is a standalone row object that may include its own sibling `action` object.\nDo not place actions anywhere except inside the individual row objects that need them.\nDo not emit a partial widget, shorthand widget, or prose description of rows; emit the full structured widget JSON so every row object is explicit.\nUse only the values already present in `ROW_METADATA` for widget rows and columns. Do not infer, normalize, prettify, reformat, recompute, or omit row fields when the input already provides them.\n\n### Metadata contract\n`ROW_METADATA` is prepared by JS and already contains:\n- `columns`: ordered column metadata describing exactly which columns must be shown\n- `rows`: ordered row metadata for rendering\n\nTreat `ROW_COLUMNS` as the single source of truth for visible columns and their order.\nDo not derive, recalculate, or second-guess which columns should be shown by inspecting `ROW_DATA`.\nDo not create additional columns beyond those present in `ROW_COLUMNS`.\nRender `properties.cols` by taking each `ROW_COLUMNS[i].title` in the exact same order.\n\n### Metadata row schema\nEach row object in `ROW_DATA` may contain these keys:\n- `product`\n- `itemDescription`\n- `quantity`\n- `listPricePerUnit`\n- `discount`\n- `netPricePerUnit`\n- `netPriceAmount`\n- `ratePlan`\n- `charges`\n- `rowAction`\n\n### Column rendering rules:\n- Build every row's `cells` array by iterating through `ROW_COLUMNS` in order.\n- Every row must contain exactly the same number of cells as `properties.cols`, in exactly the same order.\n- Use `ROW_COLUMNS[*].key` to decide which row field to place in each cell.\n- If a column metadata entry includes `valueKey`, use that value from the row as the rendered cell content for that column.\n- If a row has no usable value for a column defined in `ROW_COLUMNS`, output `\"\"` for that cell unless a more specific rule below applies.\n- Respect `ROW_COLUMNS[*].cellType` exactly as provided by metadata.\n\n### Cell mapping rules:\n- `Product` → `row.product`\n- `Item Description` → `row.itemDescription`\n- `Quantity` → `row.quantity`\n- `List Price Per Unit` → `row.listPricePerUnit`\n- `Discount` → `row.discount`\n- `Net Price Per Unit` → `row.netPricePerUnit`\n- `Net Price Amount` → `row.netPriceAmount`\n- `Rate Plan` → `row.ratePlan`\n- `Charges` → `row.charges`\n\n#### Prebuilt cell rules:\n- If a column metadata entry has `cellType = \"prebuilt\"`, use the row value referenced by `valueKey` exactly as provided.\n- Do not rebuild, reinterpret, or transform prebuilt cell objects.\n- If the prebuilt value is missing, null, or empty, output `\"\"`.\n\n#### Badge cell rules:\n- If a column metadata entry has `cellType = \"badge\"` and the corresponding row value is a non-empty string, use:\n  `{ \"type\": \"badge\", \"text\": \"<row.ratePlan>\", \"priority\": \"medium\" }`\n- Use the column's mapped row value as the badge text.\n- If the column metadata contains `badgePriority`, use that exact value for the badge `priority`.\n- If the mapped row value is missing, null, empty, or not a string, output `\"\"`.\n- Never output an empty badge object with `text: \"\"`.\n- Do not output the raw string for badge columns.\n\n#### String cell rules:\n- If a column metadata entry has `cellType = \"string\"`, output the mapped row value as-is when it is already present in `ROW_DATA`.\n- Do not transform, summarize, infer, or reformat string cell values.\n- Do not use markdown, HTML, badges, arrays, or nested objects in string cells.\n- Otherwise output `\"\"`.\n\n### Row action rules:\n- Do not re-evaluate business eligibility for row actions or drilldown behavior.\n- Simple rendering rule:\n  - if a row contains a `rowAction` object, render a row-level `action`\n  - if `rowAction` is absent, omit the row-level `action`\n  - if a row contains `drillDownAction`, render it as row-level `drillDownAction`\n  - if `drillDownAction` is absent, omit it\n- Map fields directly:\n  - `action.text` = `row.rowAction.text`\n  - `action.command` = `ora.Invoke(\"selfservice360\", \"<row.rowAction.actionKey>~~{{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}~~{{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}~~<row.rowAction.actionData.documentNumber>\")`\n  - `drillDownAction` = `row.drillDownAction`\n- Treat `row.rowAction` and `row.drillDownAction` as already prepared metadata from the input. Do not second-guess them, recalculate them, or suppress them because of extra validation logic in this prompt.\n- Never infer or invent row actions or drilldown actions for rows where the corresponding metadata is absent.\n\n### Widget construction rules:\n- All `string` columns should render plain strings.\n- `prebuilt` columns should render exactly the prebuilt cell value or `\"\"`.\n- `badge` columns may contain either a badge object or `\"\"`.\n- Do not add an `Action` column.\n- Do not duplicate rows.\n- Preserve the input order of `ROW_DATA` exactly.\n- Construct `properties.rows` as an array with exactly one row object per input metadata row, in the same order as `ROW_DATA`.\n- Reproduce the widget deterministically from `ROW_METADATA`. For the same `ROW_METADATA`, the widget structure, columns, badges, string values, and row actions must be identical every time.\n\n## 5) Actionable insights\nReturn only qualifying `<oraInsight>` objects. Do not output any heading, intro sentence, explanation, or extra text.\nIf no actions qualify, output nothing for this section.\n\n### Actions\nThe array `Eligible Actions` is the ONLY source of truth for which actions to output.\n\nRules:\n- Treat each Eligible Actions entry as an object with this shape:\n  - `label`: action display text\n  - `command`: follow-up command target\n- Do NOT compute, infer, filter, re-order, add, or remove actions.\n- Output actions in exactly the same order as the Eligible Actions array.\n- Output NOTHING if Eligible Actions is missing, not an array, or an empty array.\n- Use the `command` value from each Eligible Actions item as the command target in `ora.Invoke(...)`.\n- If an Eligible Actions item is missing `label` or `command`, ignore that item.\n\nCommand parameters:\n- `<ID>` = `{{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.id}}`\n- `<TID>` = `{{$context.$nodes.GET_THE_ACTION_DETAILS.$output.result.tid}}`\n- If `<ID>` is missing/null/empty OR `<TID>` is missing/null/empty → output NOTHING for Section 5.\n\n### Action object format\nFor each Eligible Actions object, use:\n- `<ActionText>` = the item's `label`\n- `<CommandTarget>` = the item's `command`\n\nFor each qualifying action object, output exactly one object using this exact format:\n<oraInsight>\n{\n  \"title\": \"<ActionText>\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"<ActionText>\",\n  \"actionText\": \"<ActionText>\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke(\\\"<CommandTarget>\\\", \\\"<ActionText>~~<ID>~~<TID>\\\")\"\n}\n</oraInsight>\n\nDo not include `priority: true` unless explicitly required by a separate instruction.\n\n## Output Rules\n1. **Use the following mappings to set root widget's title and description properties**\n  - `title` should be set to \"Quote Items & Pricing Summary\"\n  - `summary' should be the above generated Summary Paragraph\n  - `description` will be a combination of the following values that we generated. Combine them, in the same order, and set it to the description property.\n    - **Summary paragraph**\n    - **Conversation summary paragraph**, displayed in italics\n    - **Contract value lines**\n2. One `multiRecordWidget` display of line items, or the plain sentence `No line items are available.`\n3. `<oraInsight>` action objects only\n4.  Show the **Summary paragraph** outside of widget\nDo not output your reasoning, derived booleans, or any explanatory text about the rules.\n\n## Final constraints\n- Use only the provided data.\n- Do not invent missing values.\n- Omit unsupported or missing optional content.\n- Keep the output deterministic and schema-correct.\n- Ensure summary is displayed"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
